      "patchedSha256": "b37f5c059f4b9fdea1aebe28e91767d3262783a1ae444a52cc992070d57fe6e4",
      "reason": "Actual Android FORTIFY caught the elapsed timer writing3 bytes into2. Allocate complete unsigned32 counter buffers and format with %u. The same text owner allocated20 bytes for the37-byte postgame name prompt, now allocated from actual string length. Actual drawAllInGame and create_objeto_texto checked-write/allocation regressions observed both original failures and final full-counter/prompt preservation."
    },
    {
      "file": "proj/src/proj.c",
      "originalSha256": "f23333a1dee23540296cf2cf7e285e4d5e77f33ada3ff0f32576df3c24c292f6",
      "patchedSha256": "9d3eee05ff9b5cc14b3ee4df11184a3ca85f305152844a71dfba93702108f495",
      "reason": "Allocate the disease-name pointer array using sizeof(*deseases), preventing startup heap overwrite. Keep the existing global char* name ABI but point it to writable AAA storage, because actual postgame alterName modifies its characters and writing the original literal crashes. The postgame Points[10] buffer formats an18-byte normal score message, and the highscore digit buffer needs an unsigned32 terminator. Allocate complete summary/digit buffers and preserve unsigned values."
    },
